  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase changes: 692.73 K, melting point of Zn; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.750$ kcal/mol. \n1180 K, boiling point of Zn; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 27.565$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-1300 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 11.700 + 1.298x $10^{-3}$ T - 1.023x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 11.700x $10^{-3}$ T + 0.649x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 1.023x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 3.889</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-692.73 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -65.060 + 2.429 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.903 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 80.750 T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -65.060 - 2.429 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 0.903 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 40.375 T^{-1} + 39.372 \\times 10^{-3} T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">692.73-1180 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -65.796 + 0.028 \\times 10^{-3} T + 0.489 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 68.150 T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -65.796 - 0.028 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T - 0.489 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 34.075 T^{-1} + 25.708 \\times 10^{-3} T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1180-1300 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -96.349 + 2.560 \\times 10^{-3} T + 0.489 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 68.150 T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -96.349 - 2.560 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T - 0.489 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 34.075 T^{-1} + 69.510 \\times 10^{-3} T$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Schaefer (103). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 K from Stuve (111). High-temperature data based on Pankratz (93). ",
    "lines_raw": [
